            <div xml:id="d349-a1">

                <pb facs="0515" n="419" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg419"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 106.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Draper to the Minister of Foreign Affairs.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1898-01-12"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 12,
                    1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: Referring to your esteemed note
                    of November 26 last, informing me that, according to assurances received by you
                    from the royal ministry of commerce, article 3 of the royal decree of January
                    26, 1897, would be, without fail, modified in order to abolish the obligation of
                    the consular visé upon the certificates of meats exported to Italy from the
                    United States, and that this promised modification would be made, doubtless,
                    before the end of the year 1897; and recurring also to our conversation on this
                    subject on Thursday last, January 6, when I had the honor of a few moments’
                    interview with your excellency; I now venture to bring the wishes of my
                    Government once more before you, and to say that a strong desire is felt at
                    Washington that the promised modification of the royal decree may soon be
                    announced.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Draper.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
